#. type: Yaml Front Matter Hash Value: description
#, no-wrap
msgid "Information about IBM Quantum on IBM Cloud logging"
msgstr ""

#. type: Yaml Front Matter Hash Value: title
#, no-wrap
msgid "Logging for IBM Quantum Compute Service"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title #
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Logging for IBM Quantum Compute Service {#logging-for-ibm-quantum-compute-"
"service}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"IBM Cloud&reg; services, such as IBM Quantum Compute Service, generate "
"platform logs that you can use to investigate abnormal activity and critical"
" actions in your account, and troubleshoot problems.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"You can use [IBM Cloud Logs Routing](https://cloud.ibm.com/docs/logs-"
"router?topic=logs-router-about), which is a platform service, to route "
"platform logs in your account to a destination of your choice by configuring"
" a tenant that defines where platform logs are sent. For more information, "
"see [About Logs Routing](https://cloud.ibm.com/docs/logs-router?topic=logs-"
"router-about).\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"You can use [IBM Cloud Logs](https://cloud.ibm.com/docs/cloud-logs) to "
"visualize and alert on platform logs that are generated in your account and "
"routed by IBM Cloud Logs Routing to an IBM Cloud Logs instance.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Locations where platform logs are generated {#locations-where-platform-logs-"
"are-generated}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"IBM Cloud Container Registry generates platform logs that are displayed in "
"your logging instances. The following table lists the locations where the "
"automatic collection of Container Registry service logs is enabled.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| Location                   | Are platform services logs available? |\n"
"|----------------------------|---------------------------------------|\n"
"| Washington, D.C. (us-east) |                  Yes                  |\n"
"| Frankfurt (eu-de)          |                  Yes                  |\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Platform logs that are generated {#platform-logs-that-are-generated}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"IBM Quantum Compute Service generates platform services logs that are "
"displayed in your logging instances for the following specific cases:\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "When the state of a job changes.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Viewing logs from the Observability page {#viewing-logs-from-the-"
"observability-page}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"For information about launching the IBM Cloud Logs interface, see "
"**Launching the UI** in the [IBM Cloud Logs "
"documentation](https://cloud.ibm.com/docs/cloud-logs?topic=cloud-logs-"
"instance-launch).\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Fields by log type {#fields-by-log-type}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"For information about fields included in every platform log, see [Fields "
"that are included in platform logs](https://cloud.ibm.com/docs/logs-"
"router?topic=logs-router-about-platform-logs#about-platform-logs-2).\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "The following fields are included in the log record.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| Field           | Type     | Description                                                              |\n"
"|-----------------|----------|--------------------------------------------------------------------------|\n"
"| logSourceCRN    | Required | Defines the account and flow log instance where the log is published.    |\n"
"| saveServiceCopy | Required | Defines whether IBM saves a copy of the record for operational purposes. |\n"
"| message         | Required | Description of the log that is generated.                                |\n"
msgstr ""
